<title>USA: Koch Oil cuts U.S. posted crude oil prices $1/bbl. [CORRECTED 20:00 GMT]</title>
<headline>Koch Oil cuts U.S. posted crude oil prices $1/bbl. [CORRECTED 20:00 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Koch Oil said it lowered the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by $1.00 a barrel, effective Friday.</p>
<p>The decrease brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $17.00 (corrects from $18.00) a barrel and West Texas Sour to $14.25 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $16.50 and Oklahoma sweet is $17.00.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1620</p>
</text>
